{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774115324,"nonce":"rNqjHt8lp4/iKpYRJIA3/tc40J0=","title":"Tauri: white title bar area — window background not set to dark theme color","message":"The Tauri app shows a white title bar strip (matching the light system theme) despite titleBarStyle=Transparent and hiddenTitle=true in tauri.conf.json. The previous fix (commit 2fabe63) set the config and added CSS padding/drag-region, but did not set the window background color.\n\nRoot cause: macOS renders the transparent title bar area with the system theme color as background. The web content starts below the title bar area, leaving a white strip visible above it.\n\nFix options:\n1. Set window background color in tauri.conf.json (if supported in Tauri 2)\n2. Set it programmatically in Rust via window.set_background_color() or similar\n3. Use decorations: false and implement a fully custom title bar\n4. Use the tauri-plugin-vibrancy or window customization API to force a dark background\n\nThe PWA had no title bar at all because Safari PWAs use the meta theme-color tag, which was already set to the dark color.","files":null}]}